// Markdownlint configuration for the OCOM Specification repository.
//
// Rules disabled below are disabled because they conflict with a
// convention already used consistently across this repository's ~370
// documents, verified directly against the actual files, not disabled
// because the rules are bad in general. See CI-DESIGN.md for the full
// review this config came out of.
//
// - MD025 (single top-level heading per document): every OCOM document
//   uses a flat "#"-level heading per section (Purpose, Definition,
//   Business Meaning, ...), separated by "---" rules, not a nested
//   H1/H2/H3 hierarchy. Core/Manifest.md alone has 18 "#" headings —
//   this is the repository's normal shape, not a defect.
// - MD041 (first line must be a top-level heading): every document
//   begins with a "<!-- nav:start -->" navigation comment block before
//   its title, by repository-wide convention.
// - MD033 (no inline HTML): the nav block *is* inline HTML —
//   "<!-- nav:start -->" / "<!-- nav:end -->" comments, present in 359
//   of 373 files.
// - MD013 (line length): specification prose is not hard-wrapped;
//   enforcing a line limit would flag ordinary paragraphs, not a real
//   structural problem.
// - MD024 (no duplicate headings): confirmed present and legitimate —
//   e.g. Models/Relationship.md has two "# Constraints" sections,
//   Models/Domain.md two "# Purpose" sections, by design, not error.
//   (Verified directly; a first, space-naive check undercounted this,
//   so the true count is at least what was found, likely higher.)
// - MD040 (fenced code blocks must declare a language): 62 existing
//   fenced blocks — mostly ASCII pipeline diagrams and worked
//   examples — have no language tag. Retrofitting 62 blocks across
//   many files is a content rewrite, out of scope for a CI-only task.
//
// - MD060 (table column style): all 385 tables in this repository write
//   the delimiter row compactly ("|---|---|") while the header and body
//   rows are spaced ("| Field | Example value |"). MD060 reads the spaced
//   rows as the table's style and then reports every pipe in every
//   delimiter row. Verified directly: 385 of 385 tables share this exact
//   shape, so this is the repository's convention, not a defect in two
//   files. GitHub caps annotations at ten, which makes the failure look
//   local when it is repository-wide. Reformatting every delimiter row is
//   a whole-repository whitespace rewrite with no reader-visible effect.
//
// - MD036 (no emphasis as heading): 113 lines across 40 documents are a
//   single emphasized sentence on its own line. Most are editorial notes
//   ("*Note on this revision: ...*") rather than headings, and the rest
//   are short bold labels inside domain overviews where a real heading
//   would break the document's flat "#"-per-section structure described
//   above. Verified directly across the repository; this is the same
//   class of decision as MD025 and MD041.
//
// Left enabled (default) because the repository was checked directly
// and found already clean against them: no hard tabs, no trailing
// whitespace, every file ends with a single final newline.
{
  "config": {
    "default": true,
    "MD013": false,
    "MD024": false,
    "MD025": false,
    "MD033": false,
    "MD040": false,
    "MD041": false,
    "MD036": false,
    "MD060": false
  },
  // "globs" here is the single source of truth for which files get
  // linted — deliberately not repeated as a `with:` input in ci.yml.
  // Verified against markdownlint-cli2's own documented config
  // discovery: this file is auto-read from the directory the tool is
  // run from, no extra flag required.
  "globs": ["**/*.md"],
  "ignores": [".github/**"]
}
